      "message": "I can replace the array with a bit mask. But the race is still there...\n\nThe race is a little tricky to fix, if I understand correctly the issue is:\n\n  Task 0: pwm_disable: using_pwm[ch] \u003d 0;\n  Task 0: pwm_disable: execute loop, and every using_pwm[i] is 0\n  Task 1: pwm_configure: using_pwm[ch] \u003d 1;\n  Task 1: pwm_configure: disable_sleep(SLEEP_MASK_PWM);\n  Task 0: pwm_disable: enable_sleep(SLEEP_MASK_PWM);\n\nIf I call interrupt_disable/enable, I need to manipulate the sleep flags manually, as enable_sleep also disables/reenables interrupts:\n\n  interrupt_disable()\n  using_pwm[ch] \u003d 0;\n  for (i \u003d 0; i \u003c PWM_CH_COUNT; i++) {\n     if (using_pwm[i])\n        goto out;\n  }\n\n  sleepmask \u0026\u003d ~SLEEP_MASK_PWM;\n\n  out:\n  interrupt_enable();\n\nAm I missing a cleaner/simpler solution?",
